# Homing is refused while RTCP compensation is on.  With it on, a B home
# sweeps the head looking for the endstop and the compensation turns that
# into an X/Z move of up to the whole tool offset - unchecked, and before
# either axis is homed - while a linear home books its result as a tool
# tip rather than a carriage position.
CONFIG multi_axis_rtcp.cfg
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
SHOULD_FAIL

# [rtcp] defaults to enable: True, so this is the state the machine comes
# up in
G28 X Y Z
